  <p>The French row is arithmetic, not an announcement: the sales open on the second Wednesday of January, moved to the first when the second falls after the 12th. Four eastern departments set their own dates.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/resources/insights/holiday-content-calendar-2026">Holiday content calendar 2026</a> counts back from each of these dates to the last day to brief and deliver. This guide covers what happens in between.</p>

  <h2>Which product photos make good sources?</h2>

  <p>The ones where you can read the label at full size. If the packshot is soft, the engine has nothing to copy, and it fills the gap itself.</p>

  <p>Pick a sharp shot with the whole product in frame and even light. Then crop it close. The Image studio resizes source pictures in your browser to 1,536 pixels on the long side before it sends them, so a small product on a wide white sweep loses its print. On an engine that takes several source pictures, add a tight crop of the label as the second one.</p>

  <p>In the Image studio, pick the job <strong>Edit an image</strong>. The ChatGPT Image engines, Nano Banana 2 and Pro, and Seedream 4.5 and 5.0 Pro take up to four source pictures. FLUX.1 Kontext Pro and Max take one. The result takes the shape of the first picture you upload, so put the packshot first and change <strong>Shape</strong> when the placement needs another.</p>

