  <p>A working example, for a candle shot on white:</p>

  <div class="prompt">
    <p class="prompt__label">Prompt example</p>
    <p class="prompt__body">Using the provided images, place the candle jar from image 1 on a dark walnut table beside a frosted window, early winter evening. Two pine sprigs and a folded gray wool scarf at the left edge, cropped by the frame. One warm lamp from the left, one soft shadow falling right.</p>
    <p class="prompt__body">Keep the jar exactly as it is in image 1: amber glass, matte black lid, the same height and width. The cream label reads "WINTER FIG" above "220 g", in the same typeface, size and position; use image 2 for its detail. Do not add text, numbers, prices, logos or a second jar.</p>
    <p class="prompt__body">The jar stands in the lower right third. Leave the upper left third empty and calm for text added later. Portrait 4:5, real photograph.</p>
  </div>

  <p>The last paragraph does two jobs. It keeps the engine from lettering a sale banner into the picture, and it reserves the place where your offer goes.</p>

  <h2>Where do the E-commerce packshot and Lifestyle product scene skills fit?</h2>

  <p>They carry the rules you would otherwise type into every prompt. Open <strong>Skills</strong>, then <strong>Catalog</strong>. Find <strong>Lifestyle product scene</strong> for the festive settings and <strong>E-commerce packshot</strong> for clean product pictures, read each one with <strong>View details</strong>, then click <strong>Add to my skills</strong>. <strong>Precise image edits</strong> is worth adding too, for runs where only the scene should move.</p>

  <p>From then on, every skill switched on for <strong>Images and video</strong> rides along when <strong>Improve with AI</strong> rewrites a prompt. The rewrite is written for the engine and the job you picked, so an edit comes back as an edit instruction. It never changes your settings. Under the box you get <strong>Prompt rewritten</strong>, a short list of what changed, and <strong>Undo</strong>. Each rewrite is a small paid call against your prepaid balance.</p>

  <p>Read the rewrite before you run it. If the sentence about the label got shorter, put it back.</p>

