  <h2>How do you make enough variations without waiting on each one?</h2>

  <p>Run them side by side. Every run in the Image studio opens its own tab, newest first, and the form empties for the next one. Start the second engine while the first renders.</p>

  <p>On the ChatGPT Image engines, ask for one to ten images from a single run and keep the best. You pay for the images that come back. The price shows before every run, and a run that fails is not charged. The Image editor and Campaigns, used in the steps below, cost nothing.</p>

  <p>When one product passes, move to the next with <strong>Reuse prompt</strong> on the tab that worked: the prompt and settings come back, you swap the source picture and the label sentence, and nothing runs until you click.</p>

  <p>Pick the launch under <strong>Campaign</strong> among the options before you start. While it stays picked, every render the page saves joins that campaign, so the season's files don't scatter across the library.</p>

  <h2>How do you check that the product survived the render?</h2>

  <p>Open the render and the packshot side by side at the same size. Go down the list. A failure on the label, the logo, the color or the shape sends the picture back for a rerun. Don't paint a label back in by hand; that turns the photograph of your product into a drawing of it.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Label text.</strong> Every word spelled as printed, in the same order, typeface and place. Nothing added.</li>
    <li><strong>Logo.</strong> Once, where it belongs, not mirrored, not repeated on a prop.</li>
    <li><strong>Color.</strong> The product matches the packshot on the same screen, glass tint and lid included.</li>
    <li><strong>Proportions.</strong> Same height to width, same lid, same edges.</li>
    <li><strong>Count.</strong> One unit, and only the parts that ship with it.</li>
    <li><strong>Scale.</strong> The size reads right against the table, the scarf, a hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Light.</strong> One direction, with the shadow falling away from it.</li>
    <li><strong>Free space.</strong> The empty area you asked for is still empty, with no invented lettering.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>No engine promises the label, and the makers say so.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">OpenAI says its image model "may occasionally struggle to maintain visual consistency for recurring characters or brand elements across multiple generations."</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: OpenAI image generation guide, the maker's own documentation, page undated, read Oct. 8, 2026.</p>

  <p>When the product keeps drifting, the ChatGPT Image engines take a <strong>Mask</strong>: a PNG whose transparent areas mark what may change in the first picture. Prepare it from the packshot, product solid and everything around it transparent, and only the scene can move.</p>

  <h2>Should the discount go inside the image or on top of it?</h2>

  <p>On top. A discount rendered by the engine is one more piece of lettering to check, it can come back misspelled, and it's frozen: when the offer gets deeper, you pay for a new render and check the product all over again.</p>

  <p>There's a second reason. Some product listings take nothing but the clean render.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Google Merchant Center wants "an unobstructed, clean view of the item for sale" and lists among the overlays it does not allow "mentions of price, discounts, or offers like 'Free shipping'."</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Google Merchant Center Help, Image link [image_link], page undated, read Oct. 19, 2026. The platform's own product image requirements.</p>

  <p>So keep the clean render as the master. Click <strong>Edit</strong> on it and the Image editor opens, free and in your browser. In <strong>Text</strong>, click <strong>Add text</strong> and type the offer into the space the prompt kept empty. Pick the <strong>Font</strong>, the <strong>Size</strong> and the <strong>Color</strong>. On a light scene, a <strong>Dark outline</strong> or a <strong>Soft shadow</strong> keeps light words readable; <strong>Highlight behind the words</strong> puts a band of color under them.</p>

  <p>Everything you add stays a separate piece until you save, so you can move it and restyle it. Then click <strong>Save</strong> and <strong>Save a copy in the Assets Library</strong>. The render stays as it was. When the offer changes on Cyber Monday, open the clean render again, type the new line and save another copy. No new run.</p>

  <p>Lettering that must live inside the scene, on a sign or a gift tag, is a different job. The <a href="/resources/how-to/readable-text-in-ai-images">Readable text in AI images</a> guide covers it.</p>

